# transition.out

Normally the state being **entered** picks the transition. When hover ends, the
element returns to `animate` with `animate`'s transition. `transition.out` lets
a state set the transition its values use when they **leave** it for a
lower-priority state instead.

```svelte
<motion.div
  initial={{ scale: 0, transition: { out: { delay: 0.6 } } }}
  animate={{ scale: 1 }}
  whileHover={{ scale: 1.2, transition: { duration: 0.15, out: true } }}
/>
```

<Example isSmall exampleUrl="/examples/transition-out">
  <TransitionOutExample />
</Example>

## `out: true`

`out: true` reuses the state's own transition on the way out, so hover end is
as quick as hover start:

```svelte
<motion.div
  animate={{ opacity: 0.5, transition: { duration: 1 } }}
  whileHover={{ opacity: 1, transition: { duration: 0.1, out: true } }}
/>
```

## An `out` transition

An object is a separate transition for leaving:

```svelte
<motion.div
  whileHover={{
    scale: 1.2,
    transition: { type: 'spring', out: { duration: 0.4, ease: 'easeOut' } }
  }}
/>
```

## `out` on `initial`

On `initial`, `out` is the transition of the mount animation only. It is used
once: later changes to `animate`, and returns from hover or tap, use their own
transitions. A mount delay no longer delays every hover end.

```svelte
<motion.div
  initial={{ opacity: 0, transition: { out: { delay: 1 } } }}
  animate={{ opacity: 1 }}
/>
```

Variant children inherit their parent's `initial` label, so they use the same
`out`. Values that `initial` doesn't change on mount aren't affected.

## Value-specific transitions

Like any transition, `out` can hold per-value overrides:

```svelte
<motion.div
  whileHover={{
    opacity: 1,
    x: 10,
    transition: { out: { delay: 0.5, opacity: { duration: 0 } } }
  }}
/>
```

## Lists of labels

With a list of variant labels, the last label that sets `out` applies to all of
the list's values, including values from labels without an `out`.

## Setting only `out`

`out` is not a transition of its own. `transition: { out: { … } }` alone keeps
the value's default transition on the way **in** (a spring for `x`, `scale`
and friends), and only changes the way out.

## Exit

`exit` always uses `exit`'s own transition. An element that exits while hovered
doesn't leave with hover's `out`.

## SSR

The [optimized appear](/docs/optimized-appear) animation follows the same rule
as the mount animation: `initial`'s `transition.out` when set, otherwise
`animate`'s own transition, otherwise the `transition` prop. The server-started
animation and the hydrated runtime agree, so nothing jumps on hydration.

## API Reference

```ts
type ValueTransition = {
  // ...
  out?: boolean | Transition
}
```

`initial` and `animate` objects accept an inline `transition` (and
`transitionEnd`) in their types.

Based on Motion's `transition.out` (Motion 14.7, #1725).
